    heading: "Knowledge Is Growing Faster Than Any One Person Can Follow"
    body: "Medical knowledge expands at a pace no clinician can fully track alone — new research, new guidelines, new treatments, published continuously across the world. Intelligent systems, applied responsibly, can help surface what is relevant at the moment it is needed, without asking any single person to hold all of it in their head. The goal is not to automate judgment. It is to reduce the noise around it, so that human expertise can focus on what only humans can do: care for people."
